[{"source" ":org/Math-Academy" "forms" [{:db/id 17592186124525 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-7b9e6797-8ad6-50af-aa3b-75e9f9aa6e0e"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-7b9e6797-8ad6-50af-aa3b-75e9f9aa6e0e" :question/id #uuid "7b9e6797-8ad6-50af-aa3b-75e9f9aa6e0e" :question/math-academy-id "q-96689" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 11 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 8 & 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ shown above. Which of the following is a basis of the eigenspace corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =7?$" :question/worked-solution "To compute the eigenvectors of a matrix, we need to find non-zero solutions of the matrix equation \n\n$$\n(A-\\lambda I)\\text{x}=0.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn our case, we have $\\lambda =7.$ So, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-\\lambda I & =[\\begin{aligned}7 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 11 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 8 & 5\\end{aligned}]-7[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 8 & -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the eigenvectors, we have to solve the corresponding homogeneous system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}0=0 \\\\ {x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+8{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we row-reduce the augmented matrix $M$ to row echelon form using Gaussian elimination, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 4 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 8 & -2 & 0\\end{aligned}] &  & {R}_{1}↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 8 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 4 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] &  & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-\\frac{1}{2}){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 8 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, there is one pivot column (the $1$st one). Thus, ${x}_{2}$ and ${x}_{3}$ are free variables. From the first equation, we obtain ${x}_{1}=-4{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}.$ So, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-4{x}_{2}+{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]={x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2},{x}_{3}\\in R.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required basis is\n\n$$\nB=\\{[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-3112cc9b-c99d-5760-8709-44ca37572265"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3112cc9b-c99d-5760-8709-44ca37572265" :answer-field/id #uuid "3112cc9b-c99d-5760-8709-44ca37572265" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f7b099a0-b60b-53de-9964-15d50b6188cc" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f7b099a0-b60b-53de-9964-15d50b6188cc" "answer-754b876d-1c1d-5fa2-8c8a-19930e540b4b" "answer-e516614c-5556-5ad9-a091-72667d82e048" "answer-1d1456d1-c217-5333-894e-c3d90b3be143" "answer-f4ce0150-7f6b-597d-9302-bb72b972307e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f7b099a0-b60b-53de-9964-15d50b6188cc" :answer/id #uuid "f7b099a0-b60b-53de-9964-15d50b6188cc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-754b876d-1c1d-5fa2-8c8a-19930e540b4b" :answer/id #uuid "754b876d-1c1d-5fa2-8c8a-19930e540b4b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e516614c-5556-5ad9-a091-72667d82e048" :answer/id #uuid "e516614c-5556-5ad9-a091-72667d82e048" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1d1456d1-c217-5333-894e-c3d90b3be143" :answer/id #uuid "1d1456d1